# Exam track — Theme: Family & Myself — Sub-lesson 3: Talking About It
# @question sentences: the examiner asks in Luxembourgish, the learner
# assembles the Luxembourgish answer (always en→lu).

@lesson F1.03 "Talking About Family"

@sentence
@question Hutt Dir Geschwëster?
@lu Jo, ech hunn ee Brudder an zwou Schwësteren.
@en Yes, I have one brother and two sisters.
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-lu Kanner

@sentence
@question Wéi heescht Äre Papp?
@lu Mäi Papp heescht Pierre.
@en My father is called Pierre.
@distractor-lu Mamm
@distractor-lu wunnt

@sentence
@question Wou wunnt Är Famill?
@lu Meng Famill wunnt zu Lëtzebuerg.
@en My family lives in Luxembourg.
@distractor-lu schafft
@distractor-lu op

@sentence
@question Sidd Dir bestuet?
@lu Jo, ech si scho zéng Joer bestuet.
@en Yes, I have been married for ten years.
@distractor-lu nach
@distractor-lu Deeg

@sentence
@question Hutt Dir Kanner?
@lu Jo, ech hunn eng Duechter an ee Jong.
@en Yes, I have a daughter and a son.
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-lu Bridder

@sentence
@question Wat maachen Är Elteren?
@lu Mäi Papp ass Chauffer a meng Mamm ass Infirmière.
@en My father is a driver and my mother is a nurse.
@distractor-lu Duechter
@distractor-lu waren

@sentence
@question Wéi al ass Äre Brudder?
@lu Mäi Brudder ass drësseg Joer al.
@en My brother is thirty years old.
@distractor-lu jonk
@distractor-lu Wochen

@sentence
@question Gesitt Dir Är Famill dacks?
@lu Jo, mir gesinn eis all Weekend.
@en Yes, we see each other every weekend.
@distractor-lu ni
@distractor-lu Mount
